thig12.1:12.1 starts: then don’t do any evil kamma,
thig12.1:12.2 starts: in open, in secret.
thig12.1:12.3 starts: But if you do or will do
thig12.1:12.4 starts: any evil kamma,
thig13.5:5.1 starts: it wouldn’t be proper for me—
thig13.5:5.2 starts: aspiring to nothingness—
thig13.5:5.3 starts: having cast off gold & silver
thig13.5:5.4 starts: to take them back.
thig13.5:18.1 starts: Because many people in the world
thig13.5:18.2 starts: are stuck in the mud of sensuality,
thig13.5:18.3 starts: unknowing,
thig13.5:18.4 starts: they don’t realize the ending of birth &
thig13.5:19.1 starts: Many people follow the path
thig13.5:19.2 starts: to bad destinations
thig13.5:19.3 starts: because of sensuality,
thig13.5:19.4 starts: bringing disease on themselves.
thig12.1:10.1 starts: The Brahman:
thig12.1:10.2 starts: and now you’ve brought me
thig12.1:10.3 starts: back to the noble.
thig12.1:10.4 starts: I give you this robe for water-ablution.
thig13.1:2.1 starts: Fragrant, like a perfumed basket
thig13.1:2.2 starts: filled with flowers: my coiffure.
thig13.1:2.3 starts: With age it smelled musty,
thig13.1:2.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:8.1 starts: Like bracelets—well-fashioned, well-finished—
thig13.1:8.2 starts: my ears were once splendid.
thig13.1:8.3 starts: With age, they droop down in folds.
thig13.1:8.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:9.1 starts: Like plantain buds in their color,
thig13.1:9.2 starts: my teeth were once splendid.
thig13.1:9.3 starts: With age, they’re broken & yellowed.
thig13.1:9.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:12.1 starts: Like rounded door-bars—both of them—
thig13.1:12.2 starts: my arms were once splendid.
thig13.1:12.3 starts: With age, they’re like dried up pāṭalī trees.
thig13.1:12.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:13.1 starts: Adorned with gold & delicate rings,
thig13.1:13.2 starts: my hands were once splendid.
thig13.1:13.3 starts: With age, they’re like onions & tubers.
thig13.1:13.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:14.1 starts: Swelling, round, firm, & high,
thig13.1:14.2 starts: both my breasts were once splendid.
thig13.1:14.3 starts: In the drought of old age, they dangle
thig13.1:14.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:15.1 starts: Like a sheet of gold, well-burnished,
thig13.1:15.2 starts: my body was splendid.
thig13.1:15.3 starts: Now it’s covered with very fine wrinkles.
thig13.1:15.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:17.1 starts: Adorned with gold & delicate anklets,
thig13.1:17.2 starts: my calves were once splendid.
thig13.1:17.3 starts: With age, they’re like sesame sticks.
thig13.1:17.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.1:18.1 starts: As if they were stuffed with soft cotton,
thig13.1:18.2 starts: both my feet were once splendid.
thig13.1:18.3 starts: With age, they’re shriveled & cracked.
thig13.1:18.4 starts: The Truth-speaker’s word
thig13.2:2.1 starts: Abundant food & drink
thig13.2:2.2 starts: you give to contemplatives.
thig13.2:2.3 starts: Now, Rohiṇī, I ask you:
thig13.2:2.4 starts: Why do you hold
thig13.2:5.1 starts: They do like to work,
thig13.2:5.2 starts: They do the best work:
thig13.2:5.3 starts: They abandon
thig13.2:5.4 starts: That’s why I hold
thig13.5:9.1 starts: murder, bondage,
thig13.5:9.2 starts: loss, grief, & lamentation.
thig13.5:9.3 starts: Many misfortunes are seen
thig13.5:9.4 starts: for those head-over-heels in sensuality.
thig13.5:21.1 starts: maddening, deceptive,
thig13.5:21.2 starts: agitating the mind.
thig13.5:21.3 starts: It’s a net cast by Māra
thig13.5:21.4 starts: for the defilement of living beings:
thig13.5:25.1 starts: I follow the path—
thig13.5:25.2 starts: eightfold, straight,
thig13.5:25.3 starts: griefless, stainless, secure—
thig13.5:25.4 starts: over which great seers
